  "precisionRules": [
    "All geometry and stages outside edge building/mapping use one thread in both artifacts; serial Delaunay generates deterministic repeated topology.",
    "Full raw native scientific JSON matches exactly: remove only parallelEdgePasses diagnostics before hashing; keep every atom label, cluster ID, orientation, point, junction, Burgers vector, length, volume and other scientific field.",
    "Timing ends after native begin (through ideal mapping); finish still runs for scientific validation, but its time is excluded from this stage comparison.",
    "Fe has only 1546 expensive staged edges, below the existing 2048-item concurrent threshold; bulk direct neighbors use the exact fast bypass and the small tail stays serial.",
    "Whole DXA speed is not inferred from these isolated phase timings; periodic parallel Delaunay tie handling and host contention can affect total timings."
